  "tagline": "A planned community from the 1960s — an office park, then neighborhoods — that voted itself into a city in 2012.",
  "summary": "Peachtree Corners was planned in the late 1960s by Paul Duke: Technology Park Atlanta for work, neighborhoods around it for home. Residents voted to incorporate in 2011, and the city that began in 2012 was at once the largest in Gwinnett County. It levies no property tax of its own. In 2019 it opened a Town Center across Peachtree Parkway from The Forum and Curiosity Lab, a test track for driverless vehicles on a public street. Seven miles of the Chattahoochee River form its northern and western edge. About 42,000 people live here; public schools are Gwinnett County's.",
