      "text": "A farming settlement called Pinckneyville grows along the road from Buford to what becomes Atlanta."
    },
    {
      "year": "1870",
      "short": "The railroad",
      "text": "The railroad is built through neighbouring Norcross, and Pinckneyville's businesses move to it."
    },
    {
      "year": "1967",
      "short": "Technology Park",
      "text": "Paul Duke begins planning Technology Park Atlanta, a campus for technology firms hiring from Georgia Tech."
    },
    {
      "year": "1968",
      "short": "Peachtree Corners",
      "text": "Duke founds Peachtree Corners, Inc. to build the homes; the first neighborhoods follow in the 1970s."
    },
    {
      "year": "2011",
      "short": "The vote",
